"""v4.0: the second edition of the generator.

A dungeon's edition is part of its code. "ember-loom-42.2" is a second-edition dungeon. A code with no suffix is a
first-edition one and builds exactly what it always built, so every old link, saved game and printed guide still
matches. New dungeons are made in the second edition.

What the second edition changes:
  - no two locked doors can hold each other's keys, and a barred door is never the only way anywhere
  - no two leaders share a special power, no two people share a first name, no trap or puzzle repeats in a dungeon
  - rooms that share a kind are told apart by where they lie (North Stores, South Stores)
  - the truth of the place leaves signs in the rooms
  - deeper lists: traps, puzzles, riddles, small details, valuables, magic, curses, powers, inns, towns
  - a campaign goes deeper into one place: its kind, doom and name hold, and magic does not repeat for six levels
One change reaches both editions, in words only: a riddle that was close to one in a novel still in copyright is
replaced by an original with the same answer."""
import re, sys
sys.path.insert(0, __file__.rsplit('/', 1)[0])
from patchlib import Patch
p = Patch(sys.argv[1])

# ---- version ----
p.rep('<span class="ver">v3.5</span>', '<span class="ver">v4.0</span>')
p.rep('· v3.5 · build 2026-11-09 ·', '· v4.0 · build 2026-11-09 ·')
p.rep('Generated by Abyssal Cartographer v3.5. Dungeon code: ', 'Generated by Abyssal Cartographer v4.0. Dungeon code: ')
p.rep('Made with Abyssal Cartographer v3.5. ', 'Made with Abyssal Cartographer v4.0. ')

# ---- both editions, words only: an original riddle in place of one too close to a novel still in copyright ----
p.rep('{q:"What has roots that nobody sees, is taller than trees, up it goes, and yet it never grows?",a:"A mountain"}',
      '{q:"I am older than the road and I do not move for it. The road goes around me, the clouds sit on me, and you grow smaller with every step you take toward my head.",a:"A mountain"}')

